QUEST STRATEGY BODY [RESEARCH-INFORMED SCAFFOLD]
Convert the giver's motive into one concrete strategy. Examples:
investigate/spy/interview; deliver something for study; use an item in the field;
obtain supplies or rare materials; remove pests; defeat a specific threat;
visit or survey a dangerous place; recover lost/stolen property;
find/check on/rescue/escort a person; capture a criminal;
treat a person or repair an object; defend a site or convoy; build/restore a fortification;
sabotage or create a diversion; gather, trade or transport resources;
obtain training material, practice a Skill or seek instruction.

Choose the strategy because it changes the relevant world state. Avoid reskinning every motive as 'kill N enemies'. Combat is only one possible method and should arise when target, law, ecology or opposition makes it appropriate.
